#: ../../source/general/helpers.rst:11
msgid "What are Helpers?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/helpers.rst:13
msgid ""
"Helpers, as the name suggests, help you with tasks. Each helper file is "
"simply a collection of functions in a particular category. There are "
":doc:`URL Helpers <../helpers/url_helper>`, that assist in creating "
"links, there are :doc:`Form Helpers <../helpers/form_helper>` that help "
"you create form elements, :doc:`Test Helpers <../helpers/text_helper>` "
"perform various text formatting routines,  :doc:`Cookie Helpers "
"<../helpers/cookie_helper>` set and read cookies, :doc:`Filesystem "
"Helpers <../helpers/filesystem_helper>` help you deal with files, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/helpers.rst:22
msgid ""
"Unlike most other systems in CodeIgniter, Helpers are not written in an "
"Object Oriented format. They are simple, procedural functions. Each "
"helper function performs one specific task, with no dependence on other "
"functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/helpers.rst:27
msgid ""
"CodeIgniter does not load Helper Files by default, so the first step in "
"using a Helper is to load it. Once loaded, it becomes globally available "
"in your :doc:`controller <../incoming/controllers>` and :doc:`views "
"<../outgoing/views>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/helpers.rst:32
msgid ""
"Helpers are typically stored in your **system/Helpers**, or "
"**app/Helpers** directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/helpers.rst:37
msgid "Loading Helpers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/helpers.rst:39
msgid ""
"The :doc:`../helpers/url_helper` is always loaded so you do not need to "
"load it yourself."
msgstr ""

