#: ../../source/general/helpers.rst:188
msgid "\"Extending\" Helpers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/helpers.rst:190
msgid ""
"To \"extend\" Helpers, create a file in your **app/Helpers** folder with "
"an identical name to the existing Helper."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/helpers.rst:193
msgid ""
"If all you need to do is add some functionality to an existing helper - "
"perhaps add a function or two, or change how a particular helper function"
" operates - then it's overkill to replace the entire helper with your "
"version. In this case, it's better to simply \"extend\" the Helper."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/helpers.rst:198
msgid ""
"The term \"extend\" is used loosely since Helper functions are procedural"
" and discrete and cannot be extended in the traditional programmatic "
"sense. Under the hood, this gives you the ability to add to, or to "
"replace the functions a Helper provides."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/helpers.rst:203
msgid ""
